 all trees taller than <code>H</code>, while trees shorter than <code>H</co=
de> remain untouched. <strong>Determine the highest possible setting</stron=
g> of the woodcutter (<code>H</code>) so that it cuts <strong>at least <cod=
e>k</code> meters</strong> of wood.</p><p>Assume the woodcutter cannot be s=
et higher than the height of the tallest tree in the array.</p><h4 id=3D"ex=
ample">Example:</h4><figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; jus=
