<p>Gradually increasing the height setting of the woodcutter from H =3D 0 t=
o H =3D 8 yields less and less wood, and our goal is to find the highest va=
lue of H that gives us at least k meters of wood.</p>
<p><strong>Determining if a height setting yields enough wood</strong><br>
We need a function that determines if any given height setting H yields at =
least k meters of wood.</p>
<p>Let=E2=80=99s name this function <strong><code>cuts_enough_wood(H, k)</c=
ode></strong>, which will calculate the total wood obtained by cutting the =
